I do the protection racket because it represents the first 15 minutes to
half hour of play.  I expect a 4-to-1 ratio of death to survival.  Death
to an early pacifist tends to come mercifully quickly, so it's not a
huge investment of time to try it.  If I'm on the way and my pet dies, I
turn into a berserker, killing everything and using every item I touch.
Sometimes this hastens death, but often it yields amazing results.  

The problem I have is not really the racket itself -- I find it very
easy and quick to get to town, often with enough money to buy two rounds
of protection, and sometimes even lucky enough to get a lot more.  And
by the time this is done, the character is pretty well equipped, for a
Zero-experience-point hero.

But soon after the protection thing is done, I usually am impatient to
start killing.  So it's level 2, 3, 4, 5, very quickly.  And this is a
problem.  The difficulty of the protection racket is in the discipline
needed to refrain from killing a lot right away.  Don't kill anything
that you don't need to eat for intrinsics.  (Going up too fast will
cause generation of lower level creatures - like floating eyes - to be 
less frequent.)

